# Project-owned R8 keep rules.
# AGP combines every file in src/*/keepRules/*.keep and passes it to R8.
#
# Convention, enforced by :app:verifyKeepRules on every `check`:
#   - Every rule statement is immediately preceded by a comment line beginning
#     "# Reason:" that names why that specific symbol must survive R8.
#   - Blanket patterns are rejected: -dontshrink, -dontoptimize, -dontobfuscate,
#     -ignorewarnings, a keep rule over a bare * or ** class pattern, and -dontwarn **.
#
# The app has no reflection yet, so the correct number of keep rules today is zero.
# When one becomes necessary, find the narrowest symbol and write it here, for example:
#
#   # Reason: <why this exact class is reached only by reflection>
#   -keep class com.example.SpecificClass { <init>(); }
#
# Never widen a rule to make a release build work; remove the reflection instead.
#
# For more details, see https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules
